{"id":"feuerwerk","lemma":"Feuerwerk","pos":"noun","rank":4054,"glosses":["fireworks"],"ipa":"/ˈfɔʏ̯ərˌvɛrk/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5d/De-Feuerwerk2.ogg/De-Feuerwerk2.ogg.mp3","gender":"n","forms":{"genitive":"Feuerwerks","plural":"Feuerwerke"},"examples":[{"text":"Hast du das Feuerwerk gesehen?","en":"Did you see the fireworks?","words":[{"g":"have","l":"haben"},{"g":"you"},{"g":"the / that"},null,{"g":"to see","l":"sehen"}]},{"text":"Wann geht das Feuerwerk los?","en":"When do the fireworks start?","words":[{"g":"when"},{"g":"to go, to walk","l":"gehen"},{"g":"the / that"},null,{"g":"rid of, free of"}]},{"text":"Sobald es dunkel wird, beginnt das Feuerwerk.","en":"As soon as it gets dark, the fireworks will start.","words":[{"g":"as soon as"},{"g":"it"},{"g":"dark"},{"g":"to become","l":"werden"},{"g":"to begin","l":"beginnen"},{"g":"the / that"},null]},{"text":"Von dort kann man das Feuerwerk gut sehen.","en":"It's easy to see the fireworks from over there.","words":[{"g":"from / of"},{"g":"there, yonder"},{"g":"can, to be able to","l":"können"},{"g":"one"},{"g":"the / that"},null,{"g":"good"},{"g":"to see"}]},{"text":"Hast du das Feuerwerk gestern gesehen?","en":"Did you see yesterday's fireworks?","words":[{"g":"have","l":"haben"},{"g":"you"},{"g":"the / that"},null,{"g":"yesterday"},{"g":"to see","l":"sehen"}]}]}